{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 16, :comments ["<b>And from there, Be'erah.</b> From there the outpouring of the wadis inclined toward the place of the well concerning which HaShem said to Moses, ״Assemble the people.״ It follows that the place of that well, which was there as a deep well not rising up, was much lower than the place where Israel was at the time of the song. And since that well ascended with them toward the bank of the Arnon, which is high, from which the wadis pour downward, they saw that the blessed El had given power to those waters to ascend, and so they began their song and said, ״Ascend, O well.״ Now, what the Sages of blessed memory recounted (Berakhot, chapter HaRo'eh) concerning the war against the Amorites — that appears to be hinted at in the phrase ״Book of the Wars of YHWH,״ and Scripture did not spell out the details of the miracles out of respect for Moses and Aaron. For they needed only to show Israel what Moses and Aaron would have made known had their conduct of the command of the blessed El been in perfection — namely, that they know that those waters which He brought forth from the rock were not natural waters drawn miraculously from some spring or river, but were supernatural: the rock was transformed into a pool of water by the will of its Creator, so that they lacked the nature of other waters, whose motion inclines toward the center. Therefore they ascended with them to a place higher than the place of their source, and all the more so when they caused the limbs of the dead to move, as the Sages of blessed memory recounted. And for this reason Moses our Master did not join in this song, whose subject was to expound what was lacking in his conduct compared to the will of his Creator, which the blessed One perfected — as it says, ״And He was sanctified through them״ — for it demonstrated the nature of those waters, which possessed a power contrary to the nature of other waters, as has been explained."], :book :numbers, :voice :sforno, :lang :en, :chapter 21, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T16:40:34.463684720Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}